---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
---
<Shell title="Our colours and identity · Project Odisha"><div class="wrap">
<div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Brand studio · vector refinement 03</p><h1>One identity.<br/><em class="highlight">Room for each language.</em></h1><p class="lead">Sea-blue words. Laterite emphasis. English and Odia with space to stand on their own.</p></div>
<p class="notice">Updated to your direction: separate English and Odia marks, Nila Sagara main headings and buttons, Mankada Pathara highlights. The book-and-boat symbol is now drawn as a clean vector, with outlined English and Odia lettering; final visual approval remains open.</p>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:15px"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Two separate signatures</p><div class="brand-grid">
<div><div class="lockup"><Brand/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>English · Project Odisha</strong>The default signature for the English website. A sea-blue wordmark, with the laterite book-and-sail symbol.</p></div>
<div><div class="lockup"><Brand language="or"/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>Odia · ପ୍ରୋଜେକ୍ଟ ଓଡ଼ିଶା</strong>A standalone Odia signature in Noto Serif Odia. The project name is rendered in Odia with the same book-and-boat emblem.</p></div></div>
<div class="screen-proof"><div><p class="eyebrow">24 px symbol proof</p><img class="small-mark" width="160" height="140" src="/assets/brand-v3/symbol-small.svg" alt="Book and boat small-size proof"/></div><div class="proof-dark"><Brand tone="reverse"/></div><p style="font-size:12px;max-width:300px">The reverse preview uses a single light colour. A simplified small-size vector omits fine page detail. The reversed signature is a separate light-colour SVG.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Colour in use</p><h2>Grounded in the sea.<br/><em class="highlight">Warmed by the earth.</em></h2><div class="palette"><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--sea)"><span lang="or">ନୀଳ ସାଗର</span><div>Nila Sagara<br/><small>#1D4658 · Main headings, wordmarks and primary buttons</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--earth)"><span lang="or">ମାଙ୍କଡ଼ା ପଥର</span><div>Mankada Pathara<br/><small>#91462F · Emphasis, sail symbol and warm accents</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--olive)"><span lang="or">ଶୁଖା ଘଷି</span><div>Sukha Ghasi<br/><small>Olive #74633B · Straw #C1A263</small></div></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="button utk-button" href="/">See the updated homepage ↗</a></div><p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:13px">The supplied “World is One” image guides the balance of colour and white space. Existing working hex values are retained, rather than claiming an exact pixel match.</p></section>
<section class="section colour-story" id="colours-of-home" aria-labelledby="colour-story-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 · Colours of home</p><h2 id="colour-story-title">Stone. Sea.<br/><em class="highlight">Hearth.</em></h2></div></div>
  <div class="colour-story-grid">
    <figure class="colour-story-art">
      <a href="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" aria-label="Open the full Colours of home card"><img src="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" width="1092" height="1440" loading="lazy" alt="Project Odisha colour story in Odia and English: red laterite, deep blue sea and round, straw-textured ghasi fuel cakes."/></a>
      <figcaption>Our current signature uses the existing sea and laterite palette.</figcaption>
      <a class="text-link" href="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" download>Download the current signature ↓</a>
    </figure>
    <div class="colour-story-copy">
      <p class="lead">A colour can hold a place in memory. Ours began with the land, the sea and the warmth of a village hearth.</p>
      <article><h3><span lang="or">ମାଙ୍କଡ଼ା ପଥର</span><br/>Mankada Pathara</h3><p>The earthy red of laterite anchors our identity in the land. It brings warmth to the book-and-sail symbol, highlighted words and accents across Project Odisha.</p></article>
      <article><h3><span lang="or">ନୀଳ ସାଗର</span><br/>Nila Sagara</h3><p>Deep sea blue carries the feeling of a coastline and an open horizon. On the website, it gives our headings, wordmarks and primary buttons their steady voice.</p></article>
      <article><h3><span lang="or">ଶୁଖା ଘଷି</span><br/>Sukha Ghasi</h3><p>Ghasi is the round, hand-flattened cooking-fuel cake made from cow dung mixed with paddy straw and dried in the sun. The Founder described its familiar shape as roughly the size of a dosa.</p><p>Its dry, fibrous surface inspired our muted olive and straw tones. The story belongs to the whole fuel cake and the village hearth—not simply to loose straw.</p></article>
      <div class="colour-story-origin"><h3>A detail worth keeping</h3><p>These references came from Founder Ahimanikya Satapathy. When an early card showed loose straw, he brought us back to the actual object: ghasi. That correction is part of our story, preserved alongside earlier designs as the identity grows.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">04 · Building an Odisha feeling</p><h2>Something to wear.<br/><em class="highlight">Something to remember.</em></h2><p class="lead">An Odia word on a favourite tee. The sea on a morning cup. A flower whose story leads back to a place.</p><div class="brand-decisions"><h3>The next refinement</h3><p>Review the proportions of these two separate signatures. Sea & Stone brings the emblem, wave rhythm and separate scripts to four product designs. Botanical motifs remain a later, researched collection.</p></div></section>
<section class="prose section" style="padding-top:0"><h2>The story keeps growing.</h2><p><a href="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" download>English vector signature</a> · <a href="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-or-colour.svg" download>Odia vector signature</a> · <a href="/assets/brand-v3/symbol-small.svg" download>Small symbol</a></p><p>The palette began with the Founder’s references to laterite, the sea and sun-dried ghasi cooking-fuel cakes. This iteration changes how those same colours work together: Nila Sagara carries the reading and actions, while Mankada Pathara supplies the warmth and emphasis.</p><p>Direction: Ahimanikya Satapathy. Earlier bilingual experiments and the original palette story remain in the project KB.</p></section>
</div></Shell>

<style>
  .colour-story{padding-top:0;scroll-margin-top:28px}
  .colour-story-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:clamp(28px,4vw,64px);align-items:start}
  .colour-story-art{margin:0;min-width:0}
  .colour-story-art img{width:100%;height:auto;border:1px solid var(--line)}
  .colour-story-art figcaption{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin:12px 0 18px}
  .colour-story-art .text-link{display:inline-block;padding-block:10px}
  .colour-story-copy{min-width:0}
  .colour-story-copy article{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:22px;margin-top:26px}
  .colour-story-copy h3{font-size:26px;line-height:1.35;margin-bottom:12px}
  .colour-story-copy [lang=or]{font-family:OdiaSerif;line-height:1.6}
  .colour-story-copy article:first-of-type h3{color:var(--earth)}
  .colour-story-copy article:last-of-type h3{color:var(--olive)}
  .colour-story-copy p+p{margin-top:12px}
  .colour-story-origin{margin-top:28px;padding:24px;background:var(--paper);border-left:3px solid var(--earth)}
  .colour-story-origin h3{font-size:22px}
  @media(max-width:800px){.colour-story-grid{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}.colour-story-art{max-width:580px;margin-inline:auto}}
</style>
